ange: destination column is mirrored across the vertical axis,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cbebaa4b/D14/0/code.py:45:# - Across examples, the visible invariant is strong: the scattered pieces always reassemble into one filled rectangle\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/67e490f4/16/code.py:34:#       - Across all frames, the same canonical hole shape may recur several\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/67e490f4/16/code.py:44:#         broadcast to all three L-holes, even across frame boundaries.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/67e490f4/16/code.py:56:#     - Keep fill colors unique across shapes to avoid hidden ambiguity.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/67e490f4/16/code.py:85:#     - At least one shape always appears in more than one frame, so cross-frame\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/67e490f4/16/code.py:129:    \"\"\"Smallest key across all rotation/flip variants.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/67e490f4/16/code.py:242:    Solve several separate frames by broadcasting one unique sprite color per shape across the whole canvas.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/67e490f4/16/code.py:255:    - The outside sprites form one global broadcast dictionary: each sprite is a unique shape-colored exemplar whose color must be copied into all same-shape holes, even when those holes are split across different frames.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/446ef5d2/D8/0/code.py:123:    - rect_col is the most common color across all piece pixels and acts as a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/62593bfd/D15/2/code.py:43:#   variant must switch to `monochromatic=True`.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cbebaa4b/D14/1/code.py:27:#    Mixing point symmetry, vertical symmetry, and horizontal symmetry across examples would be\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/67e490f4/9/code.py:42:#        * group those recovered silhouettes across the frame,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/67e490f4/9/code.py:83:#      observable across 2-3 examples.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88e364bc/D4/1/code.py:55:- Marker color is fixed globally to blue (1). This keeps the rule easy to spot across 2-4 examples and avoids an\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9aaea919/D9/0/code.py:263:    Extra columns are distributed round-robin across interior gaps first, then the two outer margins,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7c66cb00/D17/0/code.py:41:#   within one puzzle instead of relying on lucky cross-example coverage.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7c66cb00/D17/0/code.py:47:#   dominant color across both edge columns over the whole bar height.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7c66cb00/D17/0/code.py:71:#   output orientation difference is easy to compare across bars:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7c66cb00/D17/0/code.py:73:# - The marker color is shared across bars and unused elsewhere, so humans can\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cbebaa4b/D14/2/code.py:46:#   Across samples, the distinctive event is obvious: colored parts close into a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c7f57c3e/D2/1/code.py:123:    Key insight: The outer edge row is the pairing key. Scale still matters for resizing, but the correct cross-group swap is determined by matching edge-color families before toggling to the companion prototype.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/446ef5d2/D8/3/code.py:18:#   intersection is the corner cell. Example for a TL corner:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/446ef5d2/D8/3/code.py:215:    - Their implied intersection is the rectangle corner.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88e364bc/D3/1/code.py:18:does not cut across open floor anymore; it travels on the ordered ring of boundary cells. The ring\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88e364bc/D3/1/code.py:67:The legend shows a left-vs-right red placement, and across examples this repeated binary cue is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/67e490f4/10/code.py:10:#      frame cell adjacent to the hole, tunnels through the frame, continues across the outer background,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/67e490f4/10/code.py:113:    \"\"\"Smallest key across all rotation/flip variants.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/67e490f4/10/code.py:303:    - Use only the background-colored subset of that component as the fill mask, then follow the tail's color path across the whole grid to find the linked sprite color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9aaea919/D9/1/code.py:34:# - The variant is visible because the four lane slots no longer form a uniform rhythm across the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/446ef5d2/D8/2/code.py:59:# - Across examples, the distinctive 5-cell plus is easy to spot and clearly no longer sits near a corner.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/446ef5d2/D8/2/code.py:168:    - rect_col = most common color across all piece pixels; all outer rectangle edges must be rect_col.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/c7f57c3e/D2/2/code.py:130:    - bg = most common color. Four scale-1 prototype sprites appear: two cross-group pairs, where each pair shares one enclosed-hole count.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/62593bfd/D6/0/code.py:52:#     - Across examples, humans see the same top-vs-bottom sorting pattern as the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cbebaa4b/D10/2/code.py:48:#     - Only two connector roles/colors are used, repeated across all samples.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/58490d8a/D5/2/code.py:76:    - Outside that patch, separate monochrome sprites of the key colors are scattered across the background.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88e364bc/D15/0/code.py:74:#       changes across rounds.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9aaea919/D2/3/code.py:27:#    The color logic is limited to exactly two structural roles repeated across all sprites:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cbebaa4b/D11/2/code.py:38:#    odd-red templates so the visual cue repeats across examples instead of becoming arbitrary.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88e364bc/D3/3/code.