de/da515329/D17/0/code.py:65:    Grow four clockwise spiral paths from a teal cross while red blockers stay fixed.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D17/0/code.py:68:    - bg = 0 (black). One teal (8) plus-sign cross with a center hole, plus several red (2)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D17/0/code.py:79:    miniature walls. The solver therefore identifies the cross exactly as before, runs the same\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dfadab01/D8/2/code.py:37:#   Every generated sample contains at least one marker type repeated across all\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/dfadab01/D8/2/code.py:179:    - Shape identity and paint color are now split across two cues: marker hue\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7b3084d4/D1/1/code.py:273:    if FEATURE == \"cross5\":\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7b3084d4/D1/1/code.py:413:    if FEATURE == \"cross5\":\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/db695cfb/D2/1/code.py:17:#     new: the diagonal connector still behaves the same, but every trigger now emits a 4-way orthogonal cross:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/db695cfb/D2/1/code.py:55:#     - branch direction is obvious from 2-3 examples because magenta expands in axis-aligned crosses rather than diagonals\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/db695cfb/D2/1/code.py:57:#     - cross rays are prevented from overlapping earlier diagonals/rays during generation\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/db695cfb/D2/1/code.py:71:    Connect same-color diagonal endpoint pairs, then emit orthogonal cross rays from trigger pixels on those diagonals.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/db695cfb/D2/1/code.py:81:    - The diagonal backbone identifies which pixels belong to the connector, but the triggered branches switch coordinate systems and expand as axis-aligned crosses rather than diagonal continuations.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/db695cfb/D2/1/code.py:175:_TRIGGERS_PER_SEG = (0, 1)      # one cross-branch per segment keeps the output legible\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a395ee82/D7/1/code.py:222:    - The singleton colored T is both the anchor of the coarse lattice and the indicator of which translated copy must switch from T to O; the only new topology is that the lattice may connect diagonally.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/64efde09/D4/1/code.py:143:    - The floating marker dots are not absolute targets; they encode template-port identities via ray alignment with the dominant edge, and those identities transfer across every rotation/reflection of the shared sprite.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D4/3/code.py:26:#       - a full 4-arm cross with directions [U, R, D, L] launches 4 spiral agents\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D4/3/code.py:43:#         across samples rather than hidden behind one fixed branch\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/da515329/D4/3/code.py:46:#       code: row/col argmax identifies the hub of a 4-arm cross\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7b3084d4/D1/3/code.py:273:    if FEATURE == \"cross5\":\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7b3084d4/D1/3/code.py:413:    if FEATURE == \"cross5\":\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D14/1/code.py:93:    - Red line within a sprite (vertical or horizontal) → mirror payload across that axis.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/97d7923e/D8/1/code.py:21:#     non-bg top-row cells are spread across the bar field and each is locally tied\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/97d7923e/D8/1/code.py:84:    Legends are distributed across the top row: each legend is a one-column stack\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/97d7923e/D8/1/code.py:184:    distributed across the bar field instead of forming one contiguous cluster.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/db695cfb/D2/3/code.py:56:#      r=c, so the \"up branch vs down branch\" contrast is actually visible across samples.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/db695cfb/D2/3/code.py:60:#      generator. This removes messy layered intersections that would hide the one-sided\n/home/l