yu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D4/1/code.py:41:#    Every generated sample contains at least one bounce, and bounced rays keep crossing beside walls whose color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D4/1/code.py:42:#    differs from the ray color. Across 2-4 examples this should make the new rule legible: walls redirect rays\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D6/1/code.py:23:#   1. a large cross: full middle row + full middle column (9 cells)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D6/1/code.py:26:#   the resting shape (large cross), while the missing complement (corner-star)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D6/1/code.py:28:#   large cross to the far endpoint. A pre-placed large cross is already stable.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D6/1/code.py:31:#   variant: solid 5x5 at top -> top large cross, bottom corner-star\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D6/1/code.py:36:# - The two complementary results are still few and repeated across channels:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D6/1/code.py:37:#   every sample shows several large crosses and several corner-stars, which is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D6/1/code.py:39:# - The corner-star is disconnected under 4-connectivity, while the cross is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D6/1/code.py:46:#   disconnected 1-cell pieces. The new passive cross is a connected 9-cell\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D6/1/code.py:48:# - Shape detection can no longer rely on a colored top-left cell: the cross has\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D6/1/code.py:53:#   bounds and leave room for the existing crossover network.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D6/1/code.py:54:# - The 4-cell endpoint gap keeps passive large crosses detached from wires.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D6/1/code.py:57:#   of 3x3 squares, and outputs contain large crosses / four-corner clusters.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47