h a 5-cell cross,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D5/0/code.py:39:#    Every collision center is chosen away from the border so its 4-neighbor cross is fully\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D5/0/code.py:40:#    in-bounds. The generator reserves the whole cross footprint for each collision, and no\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D5/0/code.py:44:#    The blue cross is strictly more salient than the old blue dot, and the presence of at\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D5/0/code.py:47:#    cross. No color-id arithmetic or invisible ordering is used.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D5/0/code.py:62:#      only full in-bounds crosses, although the solver still clips safely for robustness.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D5/0/code.py:123:def _collision_cross(center: tuple[int, int]) -> tuple[tuple[int, int], ...]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D5/0/code.py:128:def _paint_collision_cross(out: np.ndarray, center: tuple[int, int], color: int) -> None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D5/0/code.py:130:    for r, c in _collision_cross(center):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D5/0/code.py:146:    - If multiple projectiles land on the same empty background cell, that collision creates a blue (1) explosion cross centered on the landing cell, extending 1 step in the four cardinal directions.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D5/0/code.py:148:    Key insight: Triangle orientation still reveals the hidden landing cell, but now repeated landings on the same empty spot are identified by a 5-cell blue cross rather than a single blue pixel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D5/0/code.py:188:    # Projectile landings on empty background: lone impacts are maroon, repeated impacts explode into a blue cross.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D5/0/code.py:193:            _paint_collision_cross(out, dest, 1)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/409aa875/D5/0/co