 is added: red marks crossings.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D12/3/code.py:30:#    The allowed spans are restricted to 3..5 and each puzzle reuses 2-3 span values across\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/800d221b/_variant_lib.py:195:def _layout_cross_hub() -> Layout:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/800d221b/_variant_lib.py:379:        return _layout_cross_hub()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/20270e3b/D7/0/code.py:60:# - Across examples, the merged shape is the same as the original task, but the output\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D2/0/code.py:46:#    The marker color varies across samples and is not red. In many samples red is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D9/1/code.py:243:    Paint each walled-off region with a cyclic frame pattern, then let the center color spill across walls.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D9/1/code.py:251:    - Second, inspect the finished first-pass picture: each region's deepest layer color crosses any shared wall and overwrites the neighboring region's wall-adjacent outer layer by one cell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D9/1/code.py:279:# ---- Distinct marker colors across grid ----\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/31f7f899/D5/2/code.py:56:#    Across 2-4 examples a human should see two linked effects: bars are reordered by height\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D10/0/code.py:45:#   sprite lookup code must switch from color-keyed matching to shape-keyed recolor + target-keyed placement.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D2/1/code.py:139:    - Red (2) singleton embedded in a component means: reflect payload across that pixel's row.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D2/1/code.py:140:    - Blue (1) singleton embedded in a component means: reflect payload across that pixel's column.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/20270e3b/D7/2/code.py:59:#     - Across examples, the solver still clearly \"moves plug onto base\", but the output\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/31f7f899/D5/4/code.py:16:#   several same-width monochrome vertical bars that cross the baseline and have\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/31f7f899/D5/4/code.py:62:#   Across examples, the input visibly shows different bar heights and shuffled\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/31f7f899/D5/4/code.py:69:#     identical across rows. The generator guarantees that by drawing solid\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/2c181942/D5/1/code.py:11:#     new_hub: 6x6 thick cross made from five 2x2 blocks:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/2c181942/D5/1/code.py:20:#       - C is a fifth neutral hub-center color used only to keep the cross 4-connected\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/2c181942/D5/1/code.py:27:#       - mirror symmetry across the contact axis\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/2c181942/D5/1/code.py:36:#   structural/positional: square perimeter -> radial cross arms.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/2c181942/D5/1/code.py:40:# - The neutral 2x2 center is necessary; without it the four arm colors cannot form one connected cross.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/2c181942/D5/1/code.py:48:# These are replaced by an explicit 6x6 cross detector and four arm-tip contact specs.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/2c181942/D5/1/code.py:54:# - The cross occupies 20 cells inside a 6x6 bbox and has four empty 2x2 corners, so it is visually\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/2c181942/D5/1/code.py:58:# - Exactly one near-center 6x6 thick cross exists.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/2c181942/D5/1/code.py:152:def _find_cross_hub(g: np.ndarray, bg: int):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/2c181942/D5/1/code.py:157:            # The four 2x2 corners must be background so the 6x6 bbox visibly reads as a cross.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/2c181942/D5/1/code.py:232:    hub = _find_cross_hub(g, bg)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D2/0/code.py:230:# ---- Distinct marker colors across grid ----\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D2/3/code.py:146:    - Mirror the whole sprite across that axis. Originals and red controls remain.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/1/code.py:13:#       Each target is an interior crosshair:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/1/code.py:15:#       - one short perpendicular tick crossing the rail,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/1/code.py:16:#       - a colored center pixel at the crossing.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/1/code.py:33:#       A horizontal rail on row 6 with crosshair center at (6, 9) means the marker must end\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/1/code.py:36:#       so the generator switches to one sprite per crosshair.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/1/code.py:46:#       shared orientation. The dataset still varies orientation across samples.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/1/code.py:50:#       - \"anchor is an isolated singleton\": false now, because the center is embedded in a crosshair.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/1/code.py:72:#       - crosshair centers as the destinations,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/1/code.py:78:#     That avoids clutter near the rails and keeps the new crosshair cue unambiguous.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/1/code.py:92:    Slide multi-color sprites along interior crosshair rails until their marker pixels reach the matching centers.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/1/code.py:96:    - One or more interior crosshairs: a long monochrome rail plus a short perpendicular tick, with a colored center pixel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/1/code.py:97:    - Multi-color sprites whose minority-color marker matches one crosshair center color; only the marker sits on that rail.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/1/code.py:100:    - Detect each crosshair by its long rail, then match sprites to the center pixel sharing the marker color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/1/code.py:104:    Key insight: The long internal line, not the border, now encodes the motion axis and target location; the colored crossing pixel is the destination.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/291dc1e1/D1/0/code.py:58:#    cross the masked edge row/column. The transformed variants are produced by\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/0/code.py:43:- `placeholder_colors` used to come from one crop. Now colors must be aggregated across\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/0/code.py:90:    total blocks across all frames: 6-10\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/0/code.py:165:    Key insight: The external clues are still global, but the placeholders are partitioned across several independent frames, so the solver must first assign each color to the correct frame before stamping the sprites.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5dbc8537/D4/0/code.py:36:#         across the strip thickness: left border in a vertical strip, top border in a horizontal strip;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5dbc8537/D4/0/code.py:54:#     - the target palette is small (3 colors per sample) and reused across many holes, which avoids a noisy\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D2/1/code.py:185:# ---- Distinct marker colors across grid ----\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D2/2/code.py:91:    Every non-red, non-background 4-connected component is mirrored across it.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/31f7f899/D9/0/code.py:60:#    slots share the same color. This makes the change visible across only a few\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/31f7f899/D9/0/code.py:117:    Sort vertical bars by height and redistribute them across fixed x-slots.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/2c181942/D8/0/code.py:354:        # Now verify exactly 1 valid attachment across all 4 rotations x 4 sides.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/2c181942/D8/0/code.py:358:        # We need exactly 1 such (rotation, side) pair across all possibilities.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/20270e3b/D14/2/code.py:41:#      local regularities across examples rather than too many degrees of freedom.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/20270e3b/D14/2/code.py:66:#    - Across examples, horizontal lines yield tall stacked outputs; vertical lines\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/20270e3b/D14/2/code.py:79:#         * one full straight separator line across the canvas\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/1/code.py:15:#      outline around an irregular enclosed region shaped like an L or a cross.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/1/code.py:23:#      corner of that 4 x 4 box lies outside the L/cross interior, those sprite pixels\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/1/code.py:26:#    - Shape family is limited to two visible categories: L and cross. This keeps the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/1/code.py:39:#      interior mask or they would leak across the missing corners / arms.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/1/code.py:42:#      intersection with the interior is 4-connected, non-empty, and still spans the full\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/1/code.py:47:#    - At least one placeholder is visibly truncated by the L/cross boundary, so the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/1/code.py:366:    \"\"\"Return valid slot boxes whose intersection with the irregular interior stays bbox-sized.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/1/code.py:395:    \"\"\"Build an L or cross interior mask whose valid slot count stays in range.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/1/code.py:398:        shape_type = random.choice([\"L\", \"cross\"])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/1/code.py:400:        if shape_type == \"cross\":\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/3/code.py:48:#     - Anchor colors stay limited to 1-3 and are reused across 3-5 sprites, so each sample\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/3/code.py:72:#     - The generator mixes top/bottom and left/right anchors and reuses colors across\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b9e38dc0/D8/1/code.py:26:#       This keeps the visual effect obvious across 2-4 examples without introducing arbitrary\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4a21e3da/D13/1/code.py:57:    non-local comparison across multiple candidate regions.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D2/2/code.py:211:# ---- Distinct marker colors across grid ----\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/2/code.py:28:#      repeated marker color per grid and splits that color across both anchors of its pair.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/2/code.py:49:#    - Because at least one color is reused and split across both anchors, the \"choose nearer\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/2/code.py:50:#      branch is usually demonstrated within a single grid instead of relying only on cross-grid\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/31f7f899/D9/3/code.py:29:#      Input may contain 4 bars crossing the baseline plus 2 floating 2x2 blocks in\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/31f7f899/D9/3/code.py:32:#      components crossing the baseline and matching the solid centered-rectangle bar\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/31f7f899/D9/3/code.py:60:#    - Across 2-4 examples, humans can see that the corner/edge blocks never move\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/31f7f899/D9/3/code.py:61:#      while only the baseline-crossing bars get permuted by height. That difference\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/31f7f899/D9/3/code.py:104:    - Ignore foreground distractor blocks that do not match the baseline-crossing bar\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/31f7f899/D9/3/code.py:106:    - Sort only the true bars by height and redistribute them across the original\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/2/code.py:16:#   chamber, so stamping a sprite cannot cross the divider. The left chamber and the right\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/2/code.py:28:#   targets across the two regions, making the partition visually consequential.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/2/code.py:44:#   chamber walls, so no sprite can touch or cross the divider after stamping.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/2/code.py:171:            assert len(regs) == 1 and -1 not in regs, f\"placeholder color {col} crosses a divider\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/2/code.py:334:            assert int(region_by_cell[rr, cc]) == ridx, f\"sprite for color {src_col} crosses the divider\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5dbc8537/D15/2/code.py:59:#    - The four marker corners are used repeatedly across a sample, and the rectangular cores\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4a21e3da/D5/0/code.py:26:#     the formerly disappearing quadrant now remains near the split intersection and turns green\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/2c181942/D1/1/code.py:75:# - The repeated cross-example pattern is visible: the sprite above moves to the top,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D8/3/code.py:52:  - Only one shared color is reused across the three chained groups. This is the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D8/3/code.py:54:    color per group\" habit would suppress all cross-stage interactions.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D8/3/code.py:94:  - The only color adaptation is controlled color sharing across the three linked\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D8/3/code.py:96:    reused across stages.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D8/3/code.py:60:#      least one marker color across small and large regions. Humans can therefore\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D8/3/code.py:233:# ---- Distinct marker colors across grid ----\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b9e38dc0/D1/1/code.py:28:- Across the dataset, the adjacent-side pair varies, so the multi-opening rule is still visually\n/home/